#
# Counter-example for the OWL-axiom gate backing math:ResultRoleConflation: a node typed
# BOTH math:Estimand (a structured result object — the result half of the process / result
# / claim separation) AND gmeow:Observation (the held claim). module.ttl asserts
# `math:Estimand owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation` directly, so the native DL reasoner
# forces this individual into owl:Nothing — an inconsistency the reasoned closure decides,
# not a structural heuristic. The generated `math:Estimand-shape` (`sh:not [ sh:class
# gmeow:Observation ]`) is the SHACL projection of the same axiom and also fires
# (shacl.NotConstraintComponent), a documented secondary gate.
# Back-reference: math:Estimand owl:disjointWith gmeow:Observation /
# math:ResultRoleConflation (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:conflatedEstimand a math:Estimand , gmeow:Observation .
